==Battleground==
*2 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Ragin' Gory]] spawns after 41.33 seconds<sup>1,240f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Cumulus Gallus]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**6 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**1 [[Cala Maria]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**3 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The general strategy of this level is to stall for as long as possible before the base hit, building up enough money to steamroll Cumulus and Maria, winning the stage.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Given that this is a behemoth level, Courier's effectiveness should go without saying. If it needs saying, Courier has a good matchup against literally every enemy in this level.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Pizza provides an easy counter to the Ragin' Gories at the start of the level, and continues to provide a semi-decent midrange attacker throughout the rest of the level. Use carefully as it is prone to getting demolished by Cumulus.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]: Cadaver Bear can easily oneshot the Zrocos and reasonably 3-shot the Zackie Pengs (2-shot at Lv.45).
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train's fast movement speed, Double Bounty and high damage makes it an effective option for sniping Wild Doges and getting small cash injections from random peons. Can also deal chip damage to the Cala Maria and Cumulus Gallus.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Although incapable of dealing significant damage on its own, it can act as a meatshield for other rushers and nukers such as Jelly Dumpling Cat and Bullet Train Cat, specifically to stop them from getting sniped by Cala Maria
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Despite the presence of zombies in this stage, Sniper can get a surprising amount of value pushing back Cumulus and Cala Maria from the rest of your front line. Make sure to continuously spam Cadaver BearCat or something similar to prevent it from getting sniped itself by burrowers.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Even without its true form, Slime/Jelly Dumpling can easily clear out large groups of peons and relieve some of the pressure on your meatshield lines presented by the zombies, although it is by no means required.
*Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Awakened Bahamut with talents can essentially walk over Cumulus, as long as you either aggressively meatshield or use frequent Stone Cats to prevent Cala Maria from bulldozing it.

